You have now created your Spring Boot backend.

Spring Initializr generates the project structure and dependency configuration automatically.

Understand your Spring Boot project structure
Your project should look similar to this:
 studentmanagement

 .mvn
 src

 main
 java

 com.venu.studentmanagement
 StudentmanagementApplication.java
 resources
 application.properties
 test
 pom.xml
What does each folder mean?
- src/main/java: Main Java source code.
- src/main/resources: Configuration files.
- src/test: Testing code.
- pom.xml: Project dependencies and build configuration.
- application.properties: Database and server configuration.


9. Create packages for our application
Inside com.venu.studentmanagement, create five packages.

Right-click the package → New → Package.

Create:
com.venu.studentmanagement
│
├── controller
├── service
├── repository
├── entity
└── dto


Understand their responsibilities:
Package	Responsibility
Controller	Receives user requests
Service	Contains business logic
Repository	Communicates with database
Entity	Represents database tables
DTO	Transfers data between layers

This structure is called a layered architecture.
